.nf
YASMV manual                                                 compare-traces

.ti 0
SYNOPSIS

.in 3
compare-traces <trace> <other-trace>

.ti 0
DESCRIPTION

.fi
.in 3
Compare corresponding states of two traces. Arguments may be native trace
names or quoted durable artifact IDs. Requires a loaded model; both artifacts
are replayed in the current model before comparison.

The result includes revision IDs and a page of differing states. Use the
agent trace.compare operation for explicit pagination. Native trace selection
is preserved.

.ti 0
EXAMPLES

.nf
.in 3
>> compare-traces workspace_1 workspace_2

.ti 0
SEE ALSO

.fi
.in 3
help list-traces, help select-trace, help dump-trace, help capabilities.
